    <string name="dashboard_guide_quake_title">During an Earthquake</string>
    <string name="dashboard_guide_quake_desc">1. Drop, Cover, and Hold On.\n2. Stay clear of glass windows and overhead fixtures.\n3. Do not use elevators; use stairwells.\n4. Move to an open area once shaking subsides.</string>
    <string name="dashboard_guide_tsunami_title">Tsunami Warning Procedures</string>
    <string name="dashboard_guide_tsunami_desc">1. Evacuate to high ground immediately after violent shaking.\n2. Move inland away from beaches and river mouths.\n3. Do not wait for sirens if sea water suddenly recedes.</string>
    <string name="dashboard_guide_kit_title">Emergency Grab Bag</string>
    <string name="dashboard_guide_kit_desc">Keep prepared near the exit: waterproof essential documents, 3 days of non-perishable food and water, flashlight, first-aid kit, whistle, and power bank.</string>


